WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:01.234
KENDALL ROY:<i> Yeah?</i>

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.202
Uh, Kendall.
I have Logan for you.

00:00:03.268 --> 00:00:04.437
We're holding on the tarmac.

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:06.005
Yeah, hey. So look,
I think it's pretty obvious

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:06.973
what we need to say.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:08.708
So, I'm headed straight
to Josh's compound.

00:00:09.775 --> 00:00:10.676
Tell Dad "Meep-meep."

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.345
<i> It's from</i> Road Runner.

00:00:12.978 --> 00:00:14.581
♪ (TENSE MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.415 line:0%
We were all fascinated
in the writers' room

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:18.584 line:0%
about having this opportunity
to see what it would be like

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:20.487
<i> when Kendall
 and Logan first meet.</i>

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:22.288
JOSH AARONSON:<i> So...</i>

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:24.090
JESSE ARMSTRONG:<i> It seemed
like they would only do that</i>

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.059
<i> under very particular
 circumstances.</i>

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:27.460
Hello, Son.

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:28.494
Hey, Dad.

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:30.830
There's some
very uncomfortable common ground

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.231
<i>between Kendall and Logan,</i>

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:34.834
<i> which is, for today,
they need to do the business.</i>

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.036
<i> They need to convince
 this one man,</i>

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.372
and the strain of that is
almost unbearable,

00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:41.141
but it's true for them both.

00:00:44.443 --> 00:00:48.181 line:0%
Jesse has a way
of writing the unspoken.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.051
JESSE:<i> That silence felt true.</i>

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:54.754
I think it's just too much,
too much to say.

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:59.292 line:0%
They're running
a multibillion-dollar empire.

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:02.328
Logan knows he has to do
a dance for Josh.

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:05.197
I guess I have concerns.
Can we take a walk?

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:08.067
'Cause Josh is very important.
He's a major shareholder

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.335
<i>and we don't wanna lose him.</i>

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:12.037
Logan, I think he's
a compartmentalizer.

00:01:12.171 --> 00:01:14.007
<i>So, I'm not sure it hurts him
 that much</i>

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:16.476
to turn on his available charm,

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:17.577
<i> which a lot
 of these powerful guys,</i>

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:19.212
they have some of that
in the locker.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:22.449
<i> As long as the dance is
quite formalized and ritualized,</i>

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:24.917
<i>I don't think it costs you
 too much to be involved,</i>

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:27.019
but maybe he gets pushed
a little bit further

00:01:27.119 --> 00:01:28.120
<i> than he'd like by Josh.</i>

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:31.290
End of the day, you work
for the shareholders. For me.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.492
As long as he isn't asked
for something he can't give.

00:01:33.792 --> 00:01:35.095
When is this gonna end?

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:37.830
I don't like betting
on blood feuds.

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:41.868
My father is the
gravitational force of my life,

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:44.637
<i>either in relation to him
 or in opposition to him.</i>

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:47.406
Jesse has tracked
that relationship

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:49.175
<i> very differently
 in each season.</i>

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:52.244
We've reached a point
where Logan does love his son,

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:55.381
he does think his son is
extraordinarily talented.

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:59.519
It'll be okay because he's
a good kid and I love him.

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:02.755
Okay.

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.124
Maybe he's the best one
of all of them.

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:06.192
And I think he means it.

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:09.528
My father insists that he's
proud of what I've done,

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:12.765
but I'm trying to be past that,
'cause I've seen what he is.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:15.702
Nice speeches.

00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:18.504
Yeah.

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:22.475
Well, you'll say anything to get
fucked on a date, won't you?

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.410
♪ (MUSIC INTENSIFIES) ♪

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.946
All our relationships
to our parents are complicated,

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.281
<i>and boy are they complicated
 in this family.</i>

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:31.984
Does Kendall hate Logan? Yeah.

00:02:32.084 --> 00:02:33.019
<i> Does he love him? Yeah.</i>

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:34.187
KENDALL: Dad?

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:36.356
And there's a lot more layers
below that to unpick.

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:39.992
I put you in the ground that day
and you don't get to come back.

00:02:40.492 --> 00:02:44.664
Face it, son.
(WHISPERS) You lost.

